   <h1>Cairn — Privacy Policy</h1>
-  <div class="meta">Last updated: 27 July 2026 · Cairn hiking companion app</div>
+  <div class="meta">Last updated: 14 September 2026 · Cairn hiking companion app</div>
 
   <p>This policy explains what data Cairn collects, how we use it, and the rights you have. It applies to the Cairn mobile app and the accounts you create in it. If anything below is unclear, email <a href="mailto:privacy@cairnapp.nz">privacy@cairnapp.nz</a>.</p>
 
   <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
   <ul>
-    <li><strong>Account data</strong>: name and email you provide when you sign up, plus a hashed password. If you sign in with Google or Apple, we receive the same information from those providers.</li>
-    <li><strong>Location data</strong>: GPS coordinates recorded while you are actively tracking a hike or run. We do not collect background location outside of an active session unless you explicitly enable it.</li>
-    <li><strong>Content you create</strong>: hikes, cairns (map markers), notes, and photos you attach to markers.</li>
-    <li><strong>Device diagnostics</strong>: crash logs and error breadcrumbs, tied to your account, only when you have opted in via Settings.</li>
-    <li><strong>Feedback and support</strong>: whatever you send via the in-app "Send feedback" form.</li>
+    <li><strong>Account data</strong>: the name and email associated with your account, your sign-in provider, and a hashed password when you use Cairn email sign-in. Cairn never stores your plain-text password.</li>
+    <li><strong>Location and Activity data</strong>: GPS observations, routes, distance, duration and related records while you record a Hike or Run. With your separate permission, Cairn can also use foreground location to update exploration while the app is open and no Activity is recording.</li>
+    <li><strong>Content you create</strong>: Activities, Routes, Cairns (map markers), notes, marker media, Memory points and derived explored regions.</li>
+    <li><strong>Reliability diagnostics</strong>: limited app, device, crash and event information used to diagnose failures. Diagnostic uploads remove credential-shaped values and precise coordinates from real-location events before sending. Separately gated internal QA tools may upload labelled synthetic test evidence.</li>
+    <li><strong>Feedback and support</strong>: the message, category, app version and delivery identifier you send through Cairn feedback or support.</li>
   </ul>
 
   <h2>2. How we use it</h2>
   <ul>
     <li>To provide the core features of the app — showing your hikes, syncing across devices, letting you plant and rediscover cairns.</li>
-    <li>To share your hikes and cairns with people you have explicitly added as friends. Nothing you record is shared publicly by default.</li>
-    <li>To improve the app: aggregated, anonymised counts of feature usage and crash traces.</li>
+    <li>To apply the visibility choices attached to Cairns, Activities and Routes and to support friend features.</li>
+    <li>To diagnose crashes, failed sync, Activity recording defects and other reliability problems.</li>
     <li>To reply to you when you contact us.</li>
   </ul>
 
