   <h2>4. Where your data lives</h2>
-  <p>Cairn's servers run in Alibaba Cloud (Shanghai region). Your data is stored in a MySQL database and object storage bucket in the same region. Transport is over HTTPS. Passwords are hashed with bcrypt before storage.</p>
+  <p>Cairn's servers run in Alibaba Cloud's Shanghai region. Account and product data is stored in Cairn's database and object storage. Transport to Cairn services uses HTTPS and passwords owned by Cairn are hashed with bcrypt. Where Cairn offers road-aware route reconstruction, the relevant route coordinates may be sent directly to Mapbox to request candidate map geometry; Cairn remains responsible for deciding whether that geometry represents the journey.</p>
 
   <h2>5. Your rights</h2>
   <ul>
-    <li><strong>View</strong>: everything Cairn holds about you is visible in the app.</li>
-    <li><strong>Correct</strong>: edit your name, email, and password in Settings.</li>
-    <li><strong>Reset</strong>: use "Reset my map memory" in Settings to clear location history.</li>
-    <li><strong>Delete</strong>: use "Delete account" in Settings. This opens an email to <a href="mailto:privacy@cairnapp.nz">privacy@cairnapp.nz</a> that we will action within 5 business days.</li>
-    <li><strong>Export</strong>: email us to request a copy of your data.</li>
+    <li><strong>Access and export</strong>: request a JSON copy from Settings, follow its preparation status there, and use the download link when it is ready. Ready links expire after 24 hours.</li>
+    <li><strong>Correct</strong>: edit your display name and, for Cairn password accounts, change your password in Settings. Account email is not currently changeable in the app; contact support if it is wrong.</li>
+    <li><strong>Delete exploration history</strong>: remove Memory points and derived explored regions while keeping Activities, Routes and Cairns.</li>
+    <li><strong>Delete account</strong>: request deletion in Settings. Cairn disables the account and its existing sessions immediately. You can restore server-backed data by signing in during the next seven days. After that, Cairn permanently deletes the account and account-owned product data, exports, feedback and account-linked diagnostics. Account data on the requesting device is cleared when the request succeeds; unsynced device-only data cannot be restored.</li>
   </ul>
 
